WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
Algebra.

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:02.270
Algorithm.

3
00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:05.900
Both words go back to one
scholar, al-Khwarizmi,

4
00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:08.380
writing around the year 820.

5
00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:13.620
In Baghdad, Damascus and Cairo,
hospitals treated patients free.

6
00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:19.020
And at Maragha, in 1259, scholars
founded a great observatory.

7
00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:22.380
Many of these scientists
were also religious scholars.

8
00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:26.690
So why did people who prayed five
times a day build observatories,

9
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.900
hospitals and algebra?

10
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.840
In this mission, you'll
meet pioneers of medicine,

11
00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.990
mathematics and astronomy.

12
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:40.390
Then you'll test an old story: that Muslim
science died after one famous theologian.

13
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.490
Your mission: explain why people
of prayer built observatories,

14
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.450
hospitals and algebra.
